Title: A BOY NAMED DOROTHY
Author: Pistol Taeja
Format: Manga

# PAGE 1 EXT. SUNBURY TOWNSHIP - AUTOMATON HIGHWAY - DAY

Panel 1 [BLEED] [L]
It is neither a utopia nor dystopia, only infrastructure. A landscape continuously built for their children before leaving them behind.

    NARRATION
    The United Kingdom; 2845 AD; Current Population 112,900.

    NARRATION
    Somewhere in the Sunbury Township.

    NARRATION
    The Machine does exactly what it is told.

Panel 2 [H]
Mechanical high rises, endless highways, fields and water supply. The sky is grey, oppressive.

Panel 3 [BLEED]
A cracked highway stretches into the distance. In the far background, crab machines build endlessly. No humans visible anywhere.

# PAGE 2 EXT. SUNBURY TOWNSHIP - AUTOMATON HIGHWAY - DAY

Panel 1 [V][L]
DOROTHY (44, male, suited, wide hat, steel grey hair falling to his back, eyes hidden, Executive Class) walks down the centre of the highway. A sheathed shortsword hangs at his hip, a single green eye embedded in its hilt.

His expression is unreadable. A four-legged animal of some kind by his side. 

    NARRATION
    After 38 years on the run, the man wanted for murder now walks in plain sight.
    
    NARRATION
    He will remove twelve gods from this world.

TITLE Executive Class : Enemy Of The State, | DOROTHY | Age 44

Panel 2
Beside him trots the llama CHURIN, IV ALASTAIR (brown, 4ft, alpaca x llama biomechanical), human smile, seemingly intelligent llama.

It has wide, expressive eyes.

TITLE CHURIN, IV ALASTAIR | ("Commissariat : Model Llama")

Panel 3 
In the distance, spider automatons construct a building. They weld, they lift, all unending labour of unending purpose.

# PAGE 3 EXT. SUNBURY TOWNSHIP - AUTOMATON HIGHWAY - DAY

Panel 1
Dorothy glances down at Churin.

    DOROTHY
    Little lady. Find an enemy then we can rest.

Panel 2
Churin bites at the air itself, child-like, eyes closed.

    SFX: CHOMP CHOMP

Panel 3
It shakes its head up, annoyed at the question.

Panel 4
Churin trots in front, strutting ahead down the long highway. Dorothy resumes walking behind. The giant automatons and buildings loom closer.

In the distance, three faint red lines extending from behind the buildings into the sky.

# PAGE 4 EXT. SUNBURY TOWNSHIP - INDUSTRIAL AREA - DAY

Panel 1 [BLEED]
Rusted shipping containers and collapsed scaffolding; The shadows stretch long.

Panel 2
DELHI (19, female, mint-green-haired, scrawny, terrified). A spider-machine holds her in the air against a container. An ELECTRON PISTOL slips from her holster, falling unnoticed to the ground.

TITLE "DELHI" | Age 19

    DELHI
    I was only passing through to get to the shore. Your house is disgusting!

Panel 3
Two men, THE SUNBURY BROTHERS, (thuggish, armed, cruel grins) take turns slamming a bat into the side of the girl. The Senior holds a bat to the girl's head.

    SUNBURY SENIOR
    Shut it. You have your township, I have mine. I happen to like the colour grey.

Panel 4
Sunbury Junior reaches for a missile launcher not too far. He fiddles with the mechanical settings.

    SUNBURY JUNIOR
    Besides, you're only protected within your own township. This aint it.

    SUNBURY JUNIOR
    Nobody comes here without paying the toll.

# PAGE 5

Panel 1
Delhi squirms in agony. Nowhere to run.

    DELHI
    Please stop! I'm useful, I'll build whatever you want.

Panel 2
Sunbury Senior swings his bat lazily into the container.

    SUNBURY SENIOR
    Okay. Sign over your township to my brother so he can have one again.
    
    SUNBURY SENIOR
    Then we are done.

Panel 3
Delhi is taken aback with surprise at the request.

    DELHI
    I don't have that kind of authority.

Panel 4 [INSET]
Close-up on Sunbury Junior's face. Terror.

    SUNBURY JUNIOR
    Brother?!?!

SFX: FWSSH

Panel 5
A shortsword bursts through SUNBURY SENIOR's open mouth from behind. The eye on its hilt stares directly at the reader.

SFX: THUNK